  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-wsl-power",
      "text": "DeepSeek Harness plugin: Windows power state from WSL: active power plan, battery status and sleep settings.\n\nPart of **[dsh-wsl-kit](https://github.com/173787247/dsh-wsl-kit)**.\n\n[中文说明 → README.zh.md](./README.zh.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:173787247/dsh-wsl-power\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "```\nwin_power             # active plan, battery, sleep setting\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Notes",
      "text": "Reads the active scheme with `powercfg`. `battery` is absent on desktops.\n`sleepAcSeconds` is the AC standby timeout; `0` means never."
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "- Windows with WSL, and DeepSeek Harness running inside it."
    },
    {
      "section": "Tests",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm test\n```\n\nThe unit tests run anywhere. The live tests are skipped outside WSL."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Plugin** | `dsh-wsl-power` **0.1.0** |\n| **Minimum dsh** | ≥ **0.1.2** (web UI one-shot `?token=` on Windows relay `:3081`) |\n| **Latest verified** | See [dsh-wsl-kit Compatibility](https://github.com/173787247/dsh-wsl-kit#compatibility-2026-09) (currently **`0.2.2-rc.1`**) — single source of truth for the suite |\n| **Kit set** | `full` or install alone |"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
